        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\nF(0,0)=1F(0,1)=1F(1,0)=1F(1,1)=1\\\\ \nF(0,0) = 1 \\\\\nF(0,1) = 1 \\\\\nF(1,0) = 1 \\\\\nF(1,1) = 1F(0,0)=1F(0,1)=1F(1,0)=1F(1,1)=1\nTest case 222: S=[00,01,10,11]S=[00,01,10,11]S=[00,01,10,11]. So we have 161616 pairs of (x,y)(x,y)(x,y).\nF(00,00)=2F(00,10)=2F(00,01)=2F(00,11)=2F(10,00)=2F(10,10)=2F(10,01)=1F(10,11)=2F(01,00)=2F(01,10)=1F(01,01)=2F(01,11)=2F(11,00)=2F(11,10)=2F(11,01)=2F(11,11)=2F(00,00) = 2 \\\\\nF(00,10) = 2 \\\\\nF(00,01) = 2 \\\\\nF(00,11) = 2 \\\\\nF(10,00) = 2 \\\\\nF(10,10) = 2 \\\\\nF(10,01) = 1 \\\\\nF(10,11) = 2 \\\\\nF(01,00) = 2 \\\\\nF(01,10) = 1 \\\\\nF(01,01) = 2 \\\\\nF(01,11) = 2 \\\\\nF(11,00) = 2 \\\\\nF(11,10) = 2 \\\\\nF(11,01) = 2 \\\\\nF(11,11) = 2F(00,00)=2F(00,10)=2F(00,01)=2F(00,11)=2F(10,00)=2F(10,10)=2F(10,01)=1F(10,11)=2F(01,00)=2F(01,10)=1F(01,01)=2F(01,11)=2F(11,00)=2F(11,10)=2F(11,01)=2F(11,11)=2\nTo get maximum score for pair (11,10)(11,10)(11,10), we can take P=[2,1]P=[2,1]P=[2,1].\nNow C=[1,1]C=[1,1]C=[1,1] and D=[0,1]D=[0,1]D=[0,1]. Thus, maximum score is 222.\nTest case 333: S=[000,001,010,011,100,101,110,111]S = [000, 001, 010, 011, 100, 101, 110, 111]S=[000,001,010,011,100,101,110,111].\nConsider A=001,B=110,A = 001, B = 110,A=001,B=110, and a random P=[2,3,1]P = [2, 3, 1]P=[2,3,1]. Thus, CCC and DDD can be generated as :\n\nC=AP1AP2AP3=A2A3A1=010C = A_{P_1}A_{P_2}A_{P_3} = A_2A_3A_1 = 010C=AP1​​AP2​​AP3​​=A2​A3​A1​=010.\nThe longest non-decreasing subsequence are 000000 or 010101, each having length 222.\nD=BP1BP2BP3=B2B3B1=101D = B_{P_1}B_{P_2}B_{P_3} = B_2B_3B_1 = 101D=BP1​​BP2​​BP3​​=B2​B3​B1​=101.\nThe longest non-decreasing subsequence is 010101, having length 222.\n\nThus, score of P=[2,3,1]P = [2, 3, 1]P=[2,3,1] is 222 over A=001A = 001A=001 and B=110B = 110B=110. Similarly, we find the sores of all permutations of length 333 over AAA and BBB and set F(A,B)F(A, B)F(A,B) as maximum out of those."
